  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan recognizes Xiao Mang when the light path expert enters the San Cha mountain blessed land, and names Extreme Light Gu among Xiao Mang’s holdings. Ba Gui calls Xiao Mang a huge threat on that basis.",
        "chapters": [
          389
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "char_xiao_mang",
          "loc_san_cha_mountain",
          "char_ba_gui"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Xiao Mang obtained it by robbing a tomb. It is incomplete. He can use it only three times every month; crossing that limit makes the Gu self-destruct.",
        "chapters": [
          389
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "incomplete-gu",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "At San Cha Mountain, when dog emperor Ying Ming blocks him from the bronze hall, Xiao Mang flies out through a hole in the blessed land sky and raises his hands. He activates rank four Gather Light Gu; sunlight gathers on his palms into a huge, flawless ball of light. He then activates Extreme Light Gu so the glory of the immemorial era gathers into that ball and infects it. River Under the Sun Gu, at rank five, explodes the ball into an overwhelming water of light, each drop like a fragment of the sun, as the killer move Torrential Light Stream. That river pours into the blessed land, shatters the purple barrier over the bronze hall, and continues into the hall.",
        "chapters": [
          397
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "first-cast",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
